4.3. Method Summary
We now summarize our complete method, which we call Actionable Models. Our method takes as input a dataset of trajectories D = {τ }, and outputs a goal-conditioned Q-function, Qθ(s, a, g). Note that acting greedily w.r.t. this goal-conditioned Q-function provides us with a goalconditioned policy: π(a|s, g) = arg maxa Q(s, a, g). We train this Q-function by minimizing the following loss:
